**The probe's ROWS, SUMMARY and CONTRACT blocks, and its account of the committed decode -- docstring, VERBATIM:**
~~~~
27| THE COMMITTED DECODE, as read from source (the run measures it): src/cpus/cpu_ppc_instr.c's
28| D/DS-form load/store arm lists `case PPC_HI6_LD:' among its D-form cases, takes
29| `imm = (int16_t)iword;' -- the whole low halfword, XO bits included -- and decodes
30| `case PPC_HI6_LD:   load=1; size=3; break;' without looking at XO.  Read that way, every
31| opcode-58 word is a doubleword load from RA + (DS || XO): ldu reads at EA + 1 and leaves RA
32| alone, and lwa reads a DOUBLEWORD at EA + 2.  The disassembler (src/cpus/cpu_ppc.c,
33| `case PPC_HI6_LD:  load=1; wlen = 8; mnem = "ld"; break;' under its
34| `imm = (int16_t)(iword & 0xffff);') folds XO into the displacement the same way.
  ...
58| ROWS -- 8, the row denominator:
59|     ld value       XO 0 control: MEM(EA, 8), EA = DATA + 0x10
60|     ldu value      MEM(EA, 8), EA = DATA + 0x20
61|     ldu RA after   r21 = EA = DATA + 0x20
62|     lwa value      EXTS(MEM(EA, 4)), EA = DATA + 0x88
63|     lwz value      D-form control: MEM(EA, 4) zero-extended, EA = DATA + 0x88
64|     live           li r9,0x1234 round-trips through the guest and the `reg' readback
65|     unasm census   every placed word's `unassemble' line (address, word, mnemonic, RT, RA, raw low
66|                    halfword) equals the text derived from the encoder's fields, and the line count
67|                    is part of the equality.  For opcode 58 the expected text is the disassembler's
68|                    OWN convention, `ld' with displacement (DS || XO): an OBSERVATION about the
69|                    tree's disassembler that confirms opcode, RT, RA and the raw low halfword of
70|                    each placed word -- not a check of architecture
71|     neg apparatus  the same command stream against a bogus machine TYPE exits 1 with no register
72|                    dump, so every register oracle above can go red (a bogus SUBTYPE is not
73|                    rejected, which is why the TYPE is the one made bogus)
74| 
75| SUMMARY LINES: PPC_DSFORM_RESULT=<ok>/8; PPC_DSFORM_CONTROL=OK|FAIL over ld value, lwz value,
76| live, unasm census and neg apparatus; PPC_DSFORM_SYMPTOM over ldu value, ldu RA after and lwa
77| value -- PRESENT n/m when every one of them is red, ABSENT when none is, MIXED otherwise, and
78| attributable to the decode only when CONTROL=OK; PPC_DSFORM_RED=<names>; then the sentinel
79| PPC_DSFORM_PROBE_DONE.  Exit status 1 on any red row, so a run on a build that carries the
80| defect exits 1 by design.
81| 
82| CONTRACT (clause (e)).
83|   OBSERVED: for the DS-form loads ld, ldu and lwa and the D-form lwz control, the effective
84|     address each one reads (named by the loaded value), the width and extension of what it
85|     loads, and ldu's write of EA into RA.  The other three bases are read back and printed as
86|     observations (architecturally unchanged); they are not rows.
87|   NOT CLAIMED:
88|     * the store forms std and stdu (primary opcode 62) -- a later step; this probe places no
89|       store instruction in the guest;
90|     * the illegal XO values (opcode 58 with XO 3; opcode 62 with XO 2 or 3);
91|     * the invalid update forms, ldu with RA = 0 or RA = RT;
92|     * 32-bit CPUs;
93|     * translation on (MSR IR or DR set) -- every access here is physical;
94|     * 64-bit mode (MSR SF set), an EA with a non-zero high half, displacements and bases other
95|       than the ones above, an EA that crosses a page, and the indexed forms ldx, ldux, lwax and
96|       lwaux.
97| 
98| Sentinel: PPC_DSFORM_PROBE_DONE
~~~~

**The probe's `row()` and summary logic -- VERBATIM (what a gate would read):**
~~~~
141| def row(name, got, want, note=""):
142|     assert name not in [n for n, _ in rows], "DUPLICATE ROW NAME %r" % name
143|     assert len(name) <= 15, name
144|     ok = (got == want)
145|     rows.append((name, ok))
146|     print("%-16s %-20s %-20s %-52s %s" % (name, str(got), str(want), note,
147|                                           "ok" if ok else "FAIL"))
148|     return ok
  ...
469| # ================================================================ SUMMARY + DONE
470| CONTROL = ("ld value", "lwz value", "live", "unasm census", "neg apparatus")
471| SYMPTOM = ("ldu value", "ldu RA after", "lwa value")
472| okmap = dict(rows)
473| assert len(rows) == 8 and set(CONTROL) | set(SYMPTOM) == set(okmap) \
474|     and not set(CONTROL) & set(SYMPTOM), "row set drifted from the docstring"
475| npass = sum(1 for _, ok in rows if ok)
476| red = [n for n, ok in rows if not ok]
477| nsym = sum(1 for n in SYMPTOM if not okmap[n])
478| if nsym == len(SYMPTOM):
479|     sym = "PRESENT %d/%d" % (nsym, len(SYMPTOM))
480| elif nsym == 0:
481|     sym = "ABSENT"
482| else:
483|     sym = "MIXED"
484| print("")
485| print("elapsed=%.1fs binary=%s label=%s" % (time.time() - t0, BIN, LABEL))
486| print("PPC_DSFORM_RESULT=%d/%d" % (npass, len(rows)))
487| print("PPC_DSFORM_CONTROL=%s" % ("OK" if all(okmap[n] for n in CONTROL) else "FAIL"))
488| print("PPC_DSFORM_SYMPTOM=%s" % sym)
489| print("PPC_DSFORM_RED=%s" % (",".join(red) if red else "none"))
490| print("PPC_DSFORM_PROBE_DONE")
491| sys.stdout.flush()
492| sys.exit(1 if red else 0)
~~~~

### THE STORE HALF IS NOT IN THE WITNESS -- stated plainly

No `std`, `stdu` or other opcode-62 word was executed.  Their pre-fix behaviour is PREDICTED from the source -- the arm
(section 8.2) keeps the XO bits in `imm = (int16_t)iword;` and its `case PPC_HI6_STD:  size=3; break;` ignores XO -- and is
NOT measured:

* `std` (XO 0): correct -- 8 bytes at EA, RA unchanged;
* `stdu` (XO 1): 8 bytes at **EA+1**, RA **unchanged**;
* opcode 62 with XO 2 / XO 3 (illegal): 8 bytes at **EA+2** / **EA+3**, as if `std`.

**The round's detector must ROW the store forms and measure those rows RED on the BASE binary before the fix lands** --
the T36 precedent: `#570` ran its FINAL 31-row instrument on the pre-fix HEAD binary and preserved the run as
`regress/artifacts/m88kbuserrregs/table1_20261023/prefix_HEAD.out`, whose summary reads, VERBATIM:
~~~~
M88K_BUSERR_RESULT=21/31
M88K_BUSERR_CONTROL=OK
M88K_BUSERR_SYMPTOM=PRESENT 10/10
M88K_BUSERR_REVISION=2
M88K_BUSERR_LABEL=PREFIX-HEAD-7fca7187
M88K_BUSERR_ELAPSED=0.055s
M88K_BUSERR_RED=uld pfsr,uld pfar,ust pfsr,ust pfar,vme pfsr,vme pfar,luna route,luna pfar,ifetch pfsr,ifetch pfar
M88K_BUSERR_PROBE_DONE
~~~~
Q2(a) asks which store rows, with which observable, discharge clause (a) for that half.

**The witness build, from its receipts (paraphrased; the receipts sit in this session's scratchpad, NOT under
`regress/artifacts/` -- section 12).**  A scratch copy of `build/` with the five uncommitted peer `src/` files overlaid by
their HEAD blobs and `src/cpus/*.o` removed; `make` exit 0; `gxemul -nt src/cpus/cpu_ppc_instr.c` (fresh); eleven files the
probe exercises or the fix may touch `cmp`-clean against GXEMUL-SEC (`cpu_ppc_instr.c`, `cpu_ppc_instr_loadstore.c`,
`cpu_ppc.c`, `memory_ppc.c`, `memory_rw.c`, `cpu_dyntrans.c`, `machine_test.c`, `debugger_cmds.c`, `core/memory.c`,
`opcodes_ppc.h`, `cpu_ppc.h`); binary md5 `3cd0501cf7c854e0662797ccee1fce64`, re-checked at run time with no `.MUTANT`
sentinel in the scratch tree.

