## 9. Detector-shape facts for Q3 (VERBATIM excerpts at HEAD)

**9.1 Gate 13, `regress/gate_ppc.sh`** -- its header's lesson about update forms at a zero offset, its setup and skip
points, its `#527` block shape (parse before score), the `#565` block that scores `ppc_rldicl_probe.py` by row identity,
and the NetBSD prerequisite after them:
~~~~
39| # #310's eighteen rows cover the eight float UPDATE forms, every one of which
40| # stopped the emulator before this round -- neither the primary opcodes
41| # 0x31/0x33/0x35/0x37 nor the indexed 567/631/695/759 were defined or decoded.
42| # Each form gets BOTH halves of its contract: a value row and a base-register
43| # row. A diff-review seat caught the first version giving five forms a base row
44| # only, which would have passed an implementation with the wrong transfer size
45| # that still advanced the base.
46| #
47| # The two non-update rows assert the mirror image, that the base is UNCHANGED --
48| # and their displacement and index are NONZERO on purpose. With a zero offset
49| # the effective address equals the base, so a wrongly-updating implementation
50| # would write back exactly the value the row expects: the same seat found both
51| # controls vacuous that way.
  ...
 94| set -u
 95| cd "$(dirname "$0")"
 96| . ./lib.sh
 97| 
 98| gate_begin "gate 13: PowerPC FP conversion + FPSCR (#304/#305/#324-#330) + rlwimi/rldimi/rldicl"
 99| 
100| PMAX=${PMAX:-$ROOT/build/gxemul}
101| LOG=$LOGDIR/gate_ppc.log
102| 
103| need_exec "$PMAX"
104| command -v python3 >/dev/null || gate_skip "python3 not available"
105| 
106| # ---- ppcrlwimiwidth: X(rlwimi) at 32-bit width + the wrapping mask's high half --------
107| # BEFORE the NetBSD prerequisite ON PURPOSE.  These rows are register-to-register on
108| # `-E bareppc -M 64` and need no image; behind need_file a missing image would turn a
109| # red detector into a silent SKIP.  Placed here, a red row is recorded first, and #371's
110| # gate_skip then reports FAIL rather than absorbing it.  PARSE BEFORE SCORE: gates grep
111| # the result line, never the exit status, and a missing or DUPLICATED protocol line is a
112| # FAIL.  Both halves of the score are pinned to a literal so a shrunk table cannot pass.
113| RLWLOG=$LOGDIR/ppc_rlwimi.log
114| python3 ppc_rlwimi_probe.py "$PMAX" gate > "$RLWLOG" 2>&1 || true
115| #  Each KEY must occur exactly once in ANY form, and that one line must be well formed --
116| #  counting only well-formed lines let a malformed EXTRA `RESULT=' through (codex review).
117| rlwres=$(grep -c '^PPC_RLWIMI_RESULT=' "$RLWLOG")
118| rlwresok=$(grep -cE '^PPC_RLWIMI_RESULT=[0-9]+/[0-9]+$' "$RLWLOG")
119| rlwctl=$(grep -c '^PPC_RLWIMI_CONTROL=' "$RLWLOG")
120| rlwctlok=$(grep -cE '^PPC_RLWIMI_CONTROL=(OK|FAIL)$' "$RLWLOG")
121| rlwdone=$(grep -c '^PPC_RLWIMI_PROBE_DONE' "$RLWLOG")
122| if [ "$rlwres" = 1 ] && [ "$rlwresok" = 1 ] && [ "$rlwctl" = 1 ] && [ "$rlwctlok" = 1 ] &&
123|    [ "$rlwdone" = 1 ] && grep -qx 'PPC_RLWIMI_PROBE_DONE' "$RLWLOG"; then
124|     check "rlwimi protocol parsed" "yes" "yes"
125|     grep -E " ok$| FAIL$" "$RLWLOG" | sed 's/^/       /'
126|     rlw=$(grep '^PPC_RLWIMI_RESULT=' "$RLWLOG" | cut -d= -f2)
127|     check "rlwimi controls prove the probe measures" \
128|           "$(grep '^PPC_RLWIMI_CONTROL=' "$RLWLOG" | cut -d= -f2)" "OK"
129|     check "rlwimi rows run"     "${rlw#*/}" 28
130|     check "rlwimi rows correct" "${rlw%/*}" 28
131| else
132|     note "rlwimi: protocol lines missing or duplicated (result=$rlwres control=$rlwctl done=$rlwdone)"
133|     tail -5 "$RLWLOG" | sed 's/^/       /'
134|     check "rlwimi protocol parsed" "no" "yes"
135| fi
  ...
162| # ---- ppcrldiclzero (#522) + #565: X(rldicl) wrote ZERO on every execution -- its 24-row detector --------
163| # Shipped EXEMPT with e777ff06 (2026-09-10) and re-dated three times by owner ruling (2026-09-18 with
164| # ten others, eec0f4a3; 2026-09-24 with nine others; 04f3e7c0 on 2026-10-09) because no block here
165| # scored it; #565 discharges that exemption.  BEFORE the NetBSD prerequisite for the reason the rlwimi block gives: `-E bareppc -M 64`
166| # needs no image, so a red row is recorded first.  A stalled guest cannot hang the gate: the probe's
167| # own subprocess backstops (90 s; 60 s for the bogus-machine and 32-bit sessions) turn it into
168| # failing rows.  The probe prints no RESULT/CONTROL protocol, so it is scored as gate_arm.sh scores
169| # mk48's: its completion sentinel, then EVERY row by name, then the run/green/red counts and its own
170| # SCORE line, each pinned to a literal so a shrunk or renamed table cannot pass -- 30 checks when
171| # green.  Names sit in a %-18s column and none is longer than 15, so `^name  ' cannot match a
172| # neighbour (the padded-column trap).  The rows-run line is in the form check_score_claims.py pins.
173| # CONTRACT: the block TRANSMITS the probe's verdicts and re-derives none -- each row's ok/FAIL and its
174| # SCORE come from one comparison in the probe's row(), so an edit there (Grok 4.7's `ok = True', GPT-6
175| # Astra's `>=', #565 pass 2) lets a mutant through, as it would through any block that scores only a
176| # probe's ok/FAIL tokens (some gate_arm.sh blocks also pin a got= value; this one, like mk48's, does not).
177| # The exit status is ignored on purpose: this probe exits 0 with failed rows (probeexitzero).
178| # Floor (c), measured (regress/artifacts/ppcrldiclzero/gatewire_20261018/nullmedium/): an IDENTITY
179| # BODY for X(rldicl) -- decode and retire, write nothing -- reds 11 of the 30 (identity/), and
180| # /bin/true 22 of the 30.  An absent binary reds the sentinel check in this block's scoring text, but
181| # in gate 13 need_exec turns it into a SKIP before any check.
182| RLCLOG=$LOGDIR/ppc_rldicl.log
183| python3 -u ppc_rldicl_probe.py "$PMAX" gate > "$RLCLOG" 2>&1 || true
184| if [ "$(grep -cx 'PPC_RLDICL_PROBE_DONE' "$RLCLOG")" != 1 ]; then
185|     note "ppc_rldicl: completion sentinel missing or duplicated; last lines follow"
186|     tail -5 "$RLCLOG" | sed 's/^/       /'
